    {"level":"warn","text":"Stage 6 Winkler uses a 1D beam/strip model. True 2D slab-on-grade plate behaviour still needs FE or a dedicated analytical plate solution."},
    {"level":"info","text":"Changing h recalculates both the beam stiffness EI and the EC2 effective depth d. For patch or point loading, a stiffer strip can bridge farther and develop a larger ULS moment, so As,req can increase if MEd grows faster than the lever-arm benefit."},
    {"level":"info","text":"Model interpretation is transverse strip footing: x runs across the footing width, b is the out-of-plane slice width along the wall, and patch loads should represent the wall/contact width."},
    {"level":"warn","text":"beta*L is below pi, so finite-beam behaviour matters. A numerical beam-on-Winkler solve is therefore used instead of relying on the infinite-beam shortcut."},
